the men with guns haven't come to keep  the peace  they've traveled to northern mozambique  to wage war  the region has been terrorized by  islamic insurgents for the past three  years but these troops from rwanda  think they can wipe them out  can you defeat these insurgents  that is why we're here and we've already  indicated signs that they can  and will be defeated  there are a thousand rwandans here and  they've headquartered themselves in a  camp built by french firm total  the energy giant has sunk billions into  a coastal gas project but they fled when  the militants got too close  we're being taken for a tour of the  outer perimeter of the gas facility with  these giant three meter fences  and it does look like a real fortress  we moved inland with the troops and  found that dozens of communities had  been deserted  some eight hundred thousand in this  region have been displaced  but in a village called quelemagne there  were a few who'd found the courage to  return  is this a safe place to be  the military are here  they are all around us and we are  getting help we are safe we can eat and  we can communicate with the soldiers  but the rwandans won't stay here forever  and the insurgents know these  communities well many were recruited in  places just like this  you think they will come back  if you are old like me it's hard to tell  the difference between a villager and an  insurgent they all look the same  [Applause]  call themselves ansa al-sunam one of  many groups in africa who've pledged  allegiance to islamic state and deploy  their barbaric methods  the world recognized the threat during  the battle for palmer a town used by  many who worked at totel's plant  more than 200 took shelter in the  amarula hotel when insurgents invaded  the town in march  some guests tried to make a desperate  escape  and dozens lost their lives  you can see and you can feel the anxiety  and the terror that must have built up  within the walls of this lovely hotel  it's